---
import ContentLayout from '../../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../../config';
---

<ContentLayout
	title="Privacy Policy — PhotoDays"
	description="Learn how the PhotoDays iOS and iPadOS app processes photos, progress data, analytics, diagnostics and support information."
	canonicalPath="/privacy/"
	heading="Privacy Policy"
	effective="Effective September 17, 2026"
>
	<p>PhotoDays is provided by an independent developer (“PhotoDays”, “we”, “us”). This policy explains what information the PhotoDays app and website process, why it is processed and the choices available to you.</p>

	<h2>Information you add to PhotoDays</h2>
	<p>Photos, videos, notes, albums, goals, reminders and related progress data are stored on your device. In versions that include iCloud Sync, enabling it syncs this content through your private Apple iCloud account using CloudKit so it can be available on your Apple devices. We do not operate an account system for this content.</p>

	<h2>Analytics and diagnostics</h2>
	<p>PhotoDays sends limited product analytics and crash diagnostics to help us understand onboarding conversion, feature usage, reliability, and performance. Product analytics can include app and build version, device model, operating-system version, locale, selected app language and theme, premium status, feature interactions, a pseudonymous random identifier (the anonymous RevenueCat customer identifier when purchases are enabled), a random app-session identifier, and categorical onboarding answers such as selected goal, tracking method, blockers, acquisition source, and sex. The app also records purchase-flow outcomes, storefront, currency, the displayed price, trial eligibility and the offer shown. Client-side events exclude StoreKit transaction identifiers and payment-card information. RevenueCat server-side purchase events may include store transaction identifiers and subscription history, as described below.</p>
	<p>We use <a href="https://amplitude.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Amplitude</a> for product analytics and <a href="https://sentry.io/privacy/" rel="noopener">Sentry</a> for crash and error diagnostics. Their PhotoDays projects are configured for EU processing. The Amplitude SDK in PhotoDays is configured not to collect IDFV or derive country, region, city, or DMA from an IP address. Purchase events can still include the Apple storefront country reported by RevenueCat. Sentry also uses its own pseudonymous installation identifier for session health statistics, including crash-free sessions. Reliability data is therefore disclosed as linked to an installation even though we do not attach an account, email, or name. Sentry receives technical routing context such as the current screen and onboarding step, but not the detailed onboarding-answer profile, and is configured not to send default personally identifiable information. Diagnostics cover the main app and its widget, include crash stacks, active app sessions, hangs and significant handled failures, and exclude screenshots, screen recordings, UI content, attachments and automatic network breadcrumbs. Possible operating-system watchdog terminations are reviewed separately from confirmed crashes.</p>
	<p>PhotoDays is configured not to send exact body measurements, referral codes, free-form text, URLs, photos, videos, notes, file paths, email addresses, phone numbers, or other user-created content to analytics or crash diagnostics. Analytics is first-party product measurement only: it is not used for advertising, data-broker enrichment, or tracking you across apps or websites owned by other companies.</p>

	<h2>Support messages</h2>
	<p>If you contact support, we receive the email address and message you choose to send. Bug reports and support requests can also include a text attachment with non-content diagnostics: app version, operating-system version, device model, a random support identifier, iCloud sync status, local storage usage, app language, theme and time zone. The attachment does not include photos, videos, notes or albums.</p>

	<h2>Feature suggestions</h2>
	<p>When you choose “Make a Suggestion,” PhotoDays opens a public feedback portal operated by <a href="https://canny.io/privacy">Canny</a>. If you submit feedback, comment, or vote, Canny may process the information you provide, such as your name, email address, feedback content, comments, and votes, along with technical information such as your IP address, device or browser information, cookies, and usage data. Suggestions and comments you submit may be visible publicly. Please do not include photos or other sensitive information in a suggestion.</p>

	<h2>PhotoDays website</h2>
	<p>This website does not use analytics, advertising cookies, account registration or email collection. It is hosted by GitHub Pages. GitHub may log a visitor’s IP address for security purposes. See the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener">GitHub Privacy Statement</a> for details.</p>

	<h2>Photos, camera, notifications and biometrics</h2>
	<p>PhotoDays requests access only when you use a feature that needs it. Camera and photo-library access let you capture, import, save and display media. Notification access is used for reminders and related app experiences. Biometric authentication is performed by iOS; PhotoDays receives only the authentication result and does not receive or store Face ID or Touch ID data.</p>

	<h2>Purchases</h2>
	<p>Purchases and subscriptions are processed by Apple. We use <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy-policy">RevenueCat</a> to validate purchases, restore access, and determine Premium status. RevenueCat processes an anonymous customer identifier, Apple purchase and transaction information, product and subscription status, storefront, Apple’s identifier for vendor (IDFV) when available, and technical app/device information needed to provide this service. Neither PhotoDays nor RevenueCat receives your full payment-card details from Apple. No PhotoDays account registration is required. These pseudonymous identifiers can associate activity and purchases with the same customer or device; restoring a purchase can reconnect an earlier purchase record after reinstalling the app.</p>
      <p>We use the same anonymous customer identifier for purchase-related analytics in Amplitude. RevenueCat sends subscription lifecycle events such as trial starts, purchases, renewals, cancellations, expiration and refunds to Amplitude. These events can contain store transaction identifiers, product, currency, timestamps and revenue. We do not send your iCloud account identifier, photographs, album names, notes or body measurements to RevenueCat.</p>
      <p>Amplitude and Sentry remain configured for EU processing. RevenueCat is a separate service: its terms allow processing outside your country, including in the United States. We do not represent RevenueCat as an EU-only service. See RevenueCat’s <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/dpa">Data Processing Addendum</a> for its data-transfer safeguards.</p>

	<h2>How information is used and shared</h2>
	<p>We use information only to provide app features, sync your content when requested, process purchases, respond to support, maintain security, diagnose failures and improve PhotoDays. We do not sell your personal information. Information is shared only with Apple and the service providers described above as needed for these purposes or when required by law.</p>

	<h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
	<p>Local app content remains until you delete it or remove the app. iCloud content is controlled through your Apple account and the app’s sync features. Support correspondence, feature feedback, and service diagnostics are retained only as long as reasonably necessary for support, security, legal, and product-improvement purposes. You can ask us to delete support or feature-feedback information associated with your email address. For a purchase-data request, contact support so we can identify the relevant anonymous purchase record. Records required for fraud prevention, restoring valid purchases or legal obligations may need to be retained. Deleting local photographs or uninstalling the app does not cancel an Apple subscription or automatically delete purchase records held by Apple or RevenueCat. You can manage or cancel your subscription in your Apple Account settings. For a privacy request, contact support; do not send an Apple password, verification code or payment-card details.</p>

	<h2>Your choices</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>You can deny or revoke camera, photo-library, notification and biometric permissions in iOS Settings.</li>
		<li>You can keep iCloud Sync disabled and use PhotoDays only on your device.</li>
		<li>You can delete content in the app and contact us about support information.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Children</h2>
	<p>PhotoDays is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13.</p>

	<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
	<p>We may update this policy when PhotoDays or its service providers change. The effective date above will be updated when changes are published.</p>

	<h2>Contact</h2>
	<p>For privacy questions or deletion requests, email <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.supportEmail}?subject=PhotoDays%20Privacy`}>{siteConfig.supportEmail}</a>.</p>
</ContentLayout>
